      "text": "$\\Box$\nSince $\\lfloor x \\rfloor$ is an integer, we have\n\\[1 \\leq 2x < 2 \\quad  \\Rightarrow  \\quad 1/2 \\leq x < 1.\\]Also, $\\lfloor x+2 \\rfloor = \\lfloor x + (4 + 3) \\rfloor = \\lfloor x+4 \\rfloor,$ so we have\n\\[\\lfloor \\lfloor 2x \\rfloor - 1/2 \\rfloor = \\lfloor 2x \\rfloor-1.\\]We thus want to know when\n\\[ \\lfloor 2x \\rfloor-1  = \\lfloor x+2 \\rfloor.\\]This becomes\n\\[(2n+1)-1=\\lfloor x+2 \\rfloor \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad 2n = \\lfloor x+2 \\rfloor.\\]Thus, $x+2$ is in the interval $(2n+1, 2n+2).$  This means $x$ is exactly halfway between $2n+1$ and $2n+2,$ so\n\\[x = \\dfrac{2n+1}{2} - d,\\]where $0 < d < \\dfrac12.$  Setting $x = \\dfrac{2n+1}{2} - \\tfrac12,$ we see that\n\\[\\lfloor x + 2 \\rfloor = \\lfloor 2n-1 \\rfloor = 2n-1,\\]which gives us the answer\n\\[x = \\dfrac{2n-1}{2}.\\]Because all $2n+1$ are odd integers, this means the only value of $x$ for which $2n-1 \\leq \\lfloor 2x \\rfloor-1$ is $x = \\dfrac{2n-1}{2},$ for any integer $n.$",
